ed fund for the pension is the Aviva Insured Funds Multi-Asset Plus Fund II at risk level 4 (Cautious Balanced), weighted AMC 0.41%, 100% allocation. The personal pension plan review report (P17) records the existing holdings at 10-year volatility risk level 6 (Balanced Growth). The transaction history (P11–P15) confirms the existing funds are Vanguard LifeStrategy 60% and 80%, consistent with the report's description of risk level 6 holdings. No evidence in the file contradicts the recommended action of RetainAndSwitchFunds.","discrepancies":["The report states the existing fund risk level is 6 in the rationale ('current funds have a risk level of 6'), but the internal inconsistency noted in the extraction identifies that the same funds are described elsewhere in the report as having individual risk levels of 5 (Vanguard LifeStrategy 60%) and 7 (Vanguard LifeStrategy 80%), with 6 being a blended figure — P17 records the existing holdings at risk level 6 (Balanced Growth), which is consistent with the blended figure used in the rationale, so there is no contradiction with the external evidence, but the report uses two different characterisations of the same risk internally.","The report asserts 'Lower Costs' as a rationale citing a platform charge reduction from 0.32% to 0.21%, but the derived figures and switch charges table confirm the total ongoing charge rises from 0.54% to 0.62% (an increase of 0.08% / £63 per annum) when fund charges are included. The report does not disclose the net cost increase in this rationale point, presenting a partial picture that focuses only on the platform charge reduction while omitting the fund charge increase.","The report's critical yield rationale states the recommended plan needs to grow at 2.94% per year to match the existing plan — P6 confirms the mid-growth rate used is 2.94% and the maturity value at that rate for the existing plan is £86,800, which is consistent — but the critical yield comparison is described as being before the effect of any advice charges, which the report does not make clear in the rationale text.","No alternative providers or platforms are identified in the external evidence as having been formally compared and rejected; the policy research file (P24) contains an 'Alternative Strategies' section in the file strategy template but its content is blank/empty."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The existing arrangement (Aviva SIPP AV2075926) has a clearly stated recommended outcome (RetainAndSwitchFunds) and a multi-point rationale. The majority of the rationale points are corroborated by the case file: the platform charge reduction from 0.32% to 0.21% is confirmed by P6 and P21; the risk misalignment (existing risk 6 vs agreed profile 4) is corroborated by P17 and P20; the investment selection at risk level 4 is corroborated by P20; the pension switch comparison at 2.94% mid-growth rate is corroborated by P6. The arrangement's material features (no exit penalties, no GAR, no GMP, Origo-transferable) are confirmed by P1–P5 and P8–P9, supporting the absence of any retention reason that would override the switch recommendation. However, two concerns arise. First, the 'Lower Costs' rationale is materially misleading as presented: the report highlights only the platform charge reduction (0.32% to 0.21%) without disclosing that the total ongoing charge increases by 0.08% (from 0.54% to 0.62%), adding approximately £63 per year. This is not a false-positive; the derived figures confirm the net cost position is adverse, and stating 'Lower Costs' without qualification misrepresents the true cost impact. This is a weak justification at minimum and arguably a disclosure shortfall. Second, the alternative strategies section of the policy research file (P24) is blank — no alternatives are documented as having been considered and rejected in the external evidence, though the report's own text references alternatives. The risk characterisation discrepancy (6 blended vs 5 and 7 individual) is explained by P17 confirming 6 as the recorded blended level, so the rationale's use of 6 is not contradicted by external evidence. The vulnerability overlay does not materially affect this specific requirement based on the evidence available. The 'Lower Costs' assertion contradicted by the net charge increase is the primary concern.","citations":[{"passageId":"P6","source":"Pension switch report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing pension","0.54%","£427","New solution","0.62%","£490"]},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Pension switch report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":"The charge is 0.32% of the fund value at the point of applying the charge.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P21","source":"Pension switch report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Provider","Aviva Life & Pensions UK Limited","Name","Current Aviva","Valuation:","£79,092.32","Transfer value","£79,092.32","Transfer penalty:","£0.00"]},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Personal Pension Plan review report 03-12-2025 15-17.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["12.34 10 Year Volatility","6","Balanced Growth"]},{"passageId":"P20","source":"Personal Pension Plan research report 03-12-2025 11-35.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["4","Cautious Balanced","Aviva Insured Funds Multi-asset Plus Fund II (GBP)","Aviva Life & Pensions UK Ltd","100.00"]},{"passageId":"P24","source":"A Barnes - Policy Research - 2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Alternative Strategies",""]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"A Barnes - Policy Research - 2025.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Can adviser charging be applied","Yes"]}],"issueCategories":["Weak justification","Disclosure shortfall"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

