rangement.","The existing pension risk level is described as 6 overall in the options section but as two separate funds at risk levels 5 and 7 in the Alternative Solutions section — the report uses both characterisations without reconciling them.","The research product selection and platform selection sections both record 'No additional justification text has been entered', meaning no written rationale for provider/product choice was captured in the research tool beyond the filter/ranking outputs.","The report's rejection of the Vanguard funds in the Alternative Solutions section states risk mismatch against the client's 'risk profile' without explicitly naming the agreed level 4 (Cautious Balanced), whereas the options section does name level 4 explicitly — creating an inconsistency in specificity.","The fund comparison in [P11] shows HSBC Global Strategy Conservative Portfolio AC at 0.10% AMC and CT Universal MAP Cautious Fund C Acc at 0.29% AMC, both at risk level 4, yet both are cheaper than the recommended Aviva fund at 0.41%; the report does not address why the lower-cost alternatives were rejected in favour of the higher-cost recommended fund beyond the performance ranking."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The report presents a substantive set of alternatives with client-specific rejection reasons for the principal alternatives (Vanguard retention, Investment Pathways, VCTs/EIS, Investment Bonds, Cash). These reasons link to the client's agreed risk profile and stated objectives and are broadly corroborated by the research evidence. However, three material concerns arise.\n\nFirst, OPT-3 (consolidate into existing), OPT-4 (employer scheme) and OPT-5 (set up new plan) appear in the options considered section without any rejection reasons. The guard notes that options listed without individual rejection reasons are a partial answer. None of these three options is addressed in the Alternative Solutions section of the suitability report