{"groupId":"G7.10","requirement":"Benefits relied upon to justify a higher cost — are the benefits stated to justify the higher-cost recommendation supported by and consistent with the evidence in the case file?","reportSays":"The report acknowledges that the recommended pension switch results in a higher ongoing charge (0.62% vs 0.54% existing, +£63/year) and relies on five stated benefits to justify this: (1) Lower Costs — platform charge reduced from 0.32% to 0.21% via agency terms; (2) Risk Alignment — existing funds at risk level 6 are too high for the agreed Cautious Balanced profile of 4, and switching to the recommended fund aligns to risk level 4; (3) Professional Oversight — access to ongoing fund monitoring and portfolio review; (4) Tax-Efficient Contribution — £3,600 gross pension contribution utilising annual allowance with 20% tax relief; (5) Platform Integration — pension, ISA and GIA consolidated on Aviva Platform for administrative convenience. The report also states the cost justification: 'this small increase in charges is justified by the improved risk alignment and ongoing professional oversight', and provides a critical yield statement that the plan must grow at 2.94% per year (matching the mid-growth rate) to match the current plan's value, which the report asserts is achievable given improved risk alignment and professional oversight.","fileSays":"The pension switching research report [P5] confirms the agreed risk level of 4 (Cautious Balanced) and that the investment of £79,092 is being risk-rated at level 4. The suitability report itself [P21] provides a performance and volatility comparison showing the existing strategy (risk level 6 blended) against the recommended Aviva Multi-asset Plus Fund II and CT Universal MAP Cautious Fund, confirming the recommended fund demonstrates lower volatility consistent with risk level 4. The existing arrangements section [P22] confirms the existing pension holds Vanguard LifeStrategy 60% and 80% Equity funds at a blended risk level of 6, with no penalties or exit costs. The client report [P17] confirms the closing fund value of £79,092.32. The ongoing adviser charge section [P23] states the ongoing fee is 1% per annum across all Aviva Platform investments, approximately £1,558 for the year based on a total platform value of £155,812. The research reports [P1], [P2], [P3] confirm the Aviva Platform was selected and its features. The fact find [P24] confirms the client's objective of a minimum retirement income of £2,200 net per month, the desire to review and improve the pension, and interest in investment advice. No provider illustration is present in the pack (extraction notes /solution/0/illustrationProvided as NotPresentInDocument). No independent evidence of the agency terms platform charge rate of 0.21% appears in the retrieved passages — this figure appears only in the suitability report. No evidence in the pack independently confirms the critical yield of 2.94% or the mid-growth rate used. The 'Professional Oversight' benefit is generic and not client-specific. The existing plan already sits on the Aviva Platform, so Platform Integration is already available to the client without the switch.","discrepancies":["The report claims 'Lower Costs' as a benefit (platform charge reduced from 0.32% to 0.21%), but the net overall charge increases from 0.54% to 0.62% (+0.08%, +£63/year) — the report itself acknowledges this increase in the Like for Like section, creating an internal tension in presenting 'Lower Costs' as a top-level benefit heading when total costs rise.","The 'Platform Integration' benefit (pension, ISA, GIA on Aviva Platform) is stated as a justification for the higher cost, but the existing arrangement is already on the Aviva Platform (Aviva Life & Pensions UK Ltd Pension Portfolio SIPP) — this benefit is therefore already available to the client and cannot justify additional cost per the guard.","The critical yield of 2.94% is stated as equal to the mid-growth rate, with the report asserting achievability based on past performance and improved risk alignment — no provider illustration or independent projection is in the pack to corroborate this figure or the mid-growth rate used.","The 'Professional Oversight' benefit is described in generic terms and is flagged as not client-specific in the canonical model — no service proposition document or client agreement excerpt in the pack independently evidences what specific oversight services will be provided.","No independent evidence of the agency terms platform charge of 0.21% appears in the retrieved passages — the charge reduction claim is self-asserted in the report only."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The report faces a structural tension in its cost justification: it leads with 'Lower Costs' as the first stated benefit, yet the total ongoing charge rises from 0.54% to 0.62%. The report does address this transparently in the 'Like for Like' section, acknowledging the small increase and relying on risk alignment and professional oversight to justify it. However, presenting 'Lower Costs' as a benefit heading when total charges increase is potentially misleading and at minimum creates a disclosure shortfall — a client reading the benefit list may not immediately appreciate that, taken as a whole, charges are higher.\n\nThe 'Platform Integration' benefit is particularly weak. The existing pension is already on the Aviva Platform (Aviva Life & Pensions UK Ltd). The guard explicitly states that a benefit the existing plan already provides cannot justify the extra cost. Consolidation convenience is cited, but the pension itself is already on the same platform — only the ISA and GIA are new additions, and those are new products being established regardless of whether the pension switch occurs. This benefit therefore cannot legitimately justify the pension switch cost premium.\n\nRisk alignment is the strongest benefit and is corroborated by the research reports [P5] and the performance/volatility analysis in [P21], which show the existing funds carry higher risk than the agreed profile. This is a genuine, client-specific benefit.\n\nThe critical yield of 2.94% equals the stated mid-growth rate — while this appears benign (the plan only needs to match the growth rate assumed), no provider illustration is in the pack to independently confirm this figure. The assertion of achievability based on 'past performance' of the recommended funds introduces a forward-looking claim not independently evidenced in the pack.\n\nThe 'Professional Oversight' benefit is generic. The ongoing service description in [P23] lists standard services, but this appears only in the suitability report (category [I]) and cannot self-corroborate. No separate service proposition document is in the pack.\n\nThe agency terms platform charge of 0.21% is stated only in the report — no fee schedule, client agreement or provider document in the pack independently confirms this rate.\n\nOn balance: risk alignment is genuinely supported; the 'Lower Costs' framing alongside a rising total charge is a disclosure shortfall; 'Platform Integration' relies on a benefit the existing arrangement already provides; and the critical yield achievability claim and the 0.21% agency terms rate are unsupported by independent evidence. These are Potential Concerns, though the risk alignment benefit is substantive enough that this is not a high-severity finding.","citations":[{"passageId":"P22","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva Life & Pensions UK Ltd - Pension Portfolio (SIPP)","Vanguard LifeStrategy 60% Equity (35.02%) Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity (64.95%) Cash (0.03%)","6","None","Full flexi-access drawdown and UFPLS available","Over 6,900 funds available","Yes","Good platform with comprehensive facilities, but current holdings do not match agreed risk profile"]},{"passageId":"P22","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"Lower Costs - Moving to our agency terms will reduce your platform charge from 0.32% to 0.21%.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P21","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"This shows that the recommended Aviva Multi-asset Plus Fund II provides more consistent performance aligned with your Risk Level 4 profile. The fund demonstrates lower volatility than your current mix of Vanguard LifeStrategy 60% and 80% equity funds, which have a combined risk level of 6.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Pension Switching research report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["4","Cautious Balanced","£79,092"]},{"passageId":"P23","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"this small increase in charges is justified by the improved risk alignment and ongoing professional oversight.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P23","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"The costs for this service are 1% per annum across all your Aviva Platform investments. Based on current values and expected contributions, this would be equal to approximately £1,558 for the upcoming year (based on total platform value of £155,812 after initial fee deduction).","cells":null},{"passageId":"P24","source":"Fact Find (1).md","category":"B","quote":"Review his Aviva pension and look to improve upon it. Client will complete ATRQ in his own time. Wants to be fully retired by 60. Min income in retirement is £2,200 net per month.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Weak justification","Disclosure shortfall","Missing evidence"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

